fact WorkItem(id: "WI-410", description: some(value: "Stdlib: filter combinator (lazy FilteredStream carrier that provides Stream). BLOCKED on WI-356: a kept element is returned verbatim (unlike map's fn(h), whose output type comes from the transform's return), so the source head's element type must thread through splitFirst's destructured Pair — which the typer does not yet do; a head/tail workaround hits a related 'op type-param unconstrained on an abstract carrier' wall (even an explicit abstract sort-param as the type-arg reads unconstrained). Off the WI-409 critical path (WI-409 needs map+find+fold, not filter). Acceptance: filter on a List typechecks + evals; collect(filter(xs, pred)) keeps only matching elements."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-413"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-07T01:43:20Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-410", name: "first-real-map")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-410", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-07 (903a238) together with WI-413 (its only blocker). Lazy FilteredStream carrier added to combinators.anthill (sibling of MappedStream/map): entity filtered(source: Stream, pred: Function); provides Stream; splitFirst[Elem,Eff] advances the source to the first KEPT element and SELF-RECURSES on filtered(rest,pred) to skip a dropped one; filter[S,Eff](s: Stream, p) -> Stream. Both threadings work: the kept head is returned VERBATIM so its element type threads (WI-357 + the WI-413 deep-walk of the destructured Pair), and the skip-recursion's effect closes to the declared row (WI-413). ACCEPTANCE MET: eval_test wi413_lazy_filter_skips_via_self_recursion — collect(filter([1,2,3,4], n>2)) keeps [3,4] (=34), fold sums = 7, leading-skip [1,2,3]->[3]=3, all-dropped [1,2]->0, all-kept [3,4,5]=12. Uses explicit [S,Eff] like map[Dst,Eff] (output element = source element). The stale 'BLOCKED on WI-356' note was already corrected to WI-413 (f1a6a4f).", at: "2026-06-07T01:43:07Z")
